\import{fnip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fnip}
\taxon{Example}
\title{Eigenlines of a node and a saddle}
\date{2026-11-26}

\p{The upper drawing is the linear equation
##{\dot x=-x,\qquad \dot y=-3y.}
The eigenvalues are #{-1} and #{-3}, so the origin is a stable
[node](fnip-0035). The axes are the eigenlines. A solution that
starts on the horizontal axis is a multiple of #{e^{-t}}, and a
solution that starts on the vertical axis is a multiple of
#{e^{-3t}}. Every other solution lies on a curve #{y=Cx^{3}} and
approaches the origin along the horizontal axis, the eigenvalue of
smaller absolute value.}

\p{The lower drawing is the linear equation
##{\dot x=x,\qquad \dot y=-y.}
The eigenvalues are #{1} and #{-1}, so the origin is a
[saddle](fnip-0035). The axes are the eigenlines, and the other
solutions lie on the hyperbolas #{xy=C} for a nonzero constant
#{C}. Solutions
leave along the horizontal axis and approach along the vertical
axis.}

